[{"id":2934902418,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6u7w6S","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","login":"lyuma","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma"},"body":"So if I understand, the issue is that wav uses *unsigned* uint32, while Godot integers are signed when exposed in APIs (or when used in vectors). I think it makes sense....\r\n\r\nA lot of my uncertainty comes down also to code style. For example, given that Vector.resize() returns an Error, is it better to store that in a variable, and then call `ERR_FAIL_COND_V(err, ...)` , or better to do it on one line as this code is written.\r\n\r\nI would like @AThousandShips to take a look at this code and see if it's going in the right direction in terms of code quality + style. If she thinks it is good, and there's some way to verify that this fixes an issue (MRP / example case) then I think I'd be okay approving this change.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#pullrequestreview-2934902418","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107596","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-17T09:32:44Z"},{"id":2934946880,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6u77xA","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0